{"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Systems"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"Systems","role":"collection","title":"Systems","symbolKind":"module"},"sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A world holds data: entities and their components, and resources. A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"system"}]},{"type":"text","text":" holds a rule: a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"step that reads part of the world and changes part of it, such as “every entity with a velocity"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"moves” or “gravity pulls on everything that isn’t frozen.” A "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"schedule"}]},{"type":"text","text":" lists the systems of one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"frame or step and runs them on a world, each once per run."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The examples throughout this module use these components, resources and event:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["struct Position: Component { var x: Double, y: Double }","struct Velocity: Component { var dx: Double, dy: Double }","struct Health: Component { var current: Int }","struct Frozen: Component {}","","struct Score: Resource { var points: Int }","struct TimeStep: Resource { var seconds: Double }","struct Paused: Resource {}","","struct Damage: Event { var target: Entity, amount: Int }"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Declare-a-System","text":"Declare a System"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The simplest way to write a system is to mark a type with the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@System"},{"text":" macro and give it a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"run"},{"text":" method. The method’s parameters say what the system works on, and their types say how:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"an ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" writes components, a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" reads them, and a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reads a resource. The following two systems pull everything that isn’t frozen downward, then move","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"it by its velocity:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["@System","struct Gravity {","    func run(_ falling: Update<Velocity>.Where<Without<Frozen>>) {","        falling { velocity, _ in velocity.dy -= 10 }","    }","}","","@System","struct Movement {","    func run(_ movers: Update<Position>.Over<Velocity>.Where<Without<Frozen>>) {","        movers { position, row in","            position.x += row.components.dx","            position.y += row.components.dy","        }","    }","}"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Because the parameters’ types state what each system reads and writes, the macro writes the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system’s ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/access"},{"text":" for you: ","type":"text"},{"code":"Gravity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" writes ","type":"text"},{"code":"Velocity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"code":"Movement","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" writes ","type":"text"},{"code":"Position","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reads ","type":"text"},{"code":"Velocity","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A schedule uses the access to decide which systems can run at the same time.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"You can also conform a type to ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" by hand and write its ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System\/run(in:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" method, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"receives the whole world. See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for when to do that.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Run-Systems-in-a-Schedule","text":"Run Systems in a Schedule"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule"},{"text":" is built from a list of systems, written in a result builder. Running it runs each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"system once. The following example drops a ball for one frame:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["var world = World()","let ball = world.spawn(Position(x: 0, y: 100), Velocity(dx: 1, dy: 0))","","let frame = Schedule {","    Gravity()","    Movement().after(Gravity.self)","}","frame.run(on: &world)","","print(world[Position.self, of: ball])","\/\/ Prints \"Position(x: 1.0, y: 90.0)\""],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Systems run in the order you write them, unless an ordering constraint says otherwise.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"after(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"before(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" require one system to run after or before another; ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"names a group of systems so constraints can refer to all of them at once; and ","type":"text"},{"code":"runIf(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" skips","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a system when a condition doesn’t hold.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Systems whose accesses don’t conflict, because neither writes what the other reads or writes,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"run at the same time, and the world ends as though they had run one after another (commands","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"apply when each wave finishes). Systems that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conflict run in order. When two conflicting systems aren’t ordered by any constraint, their order","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rests only on how they happen to be written; ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule\/ambiguities()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" finds those pairs so a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"test can keep a schedule free of them. To learn more, see ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SchedulingSystems","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/systems"]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DeclaringSystems","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SchedulingSystems","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/DrivingAWorldFromAnApp","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System()","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/System"]},{"title":"System Parameters","anchor":"System-Parameters","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemParameter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceReader","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ResourceWriter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventReader","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/EventWriter","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/RemovedComponents"]},{"title":"Building and Running Schedules","anchor":"Building-and-Running-Schedules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduleBuilder","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemSet","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Ambiguity"]},{"title":"Main-Actor Systems","anchor":"Main-Actor-Systems","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/MainActorSystem"]},{"title":"Built-In Systems","anchor":"Built-In-Systems","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/UpdateEvents","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardEvents","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardChanges"]},{"title":"Profiling","anchor":"Profiling","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemProfile","doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemTiming"]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"Declare the rules of a simulation as systems, and run them on a world in a schedule.","type":"text"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SchedulingSystems":{"type":"topic","kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SchedulingSystems","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedulingsystems","role":"article","abstract":[{"text":"Order the systems of a schedule, run them only when a condition holds, and find out how a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"schedule runs them.","type":"text"}],"title":"Scheduling Systems"},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Update":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Update","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/update","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Update"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system parameter that changes a component of every entity that holds it."}],"title":"Update","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"class"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Update"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/CyclicOrdering":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"An error indicating that the ordering constraints of a schedule’s systems form a cycle, so no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order satisfies them all.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/CyclicOrdering","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/cyclicordering","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"CyclicOrdering"}],"title":"CyclicOrdering","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"CyclicOrdering"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/SystemTiming":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The times one system of a schedule has taken to run."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/SystemTiming","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/systemtiming","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SystemTiming","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"SystemTiming","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SystemTiming","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ScheduledSystem":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"A system together with the ordering constraints, sets and conditions a schedule runs it with.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ScheduledSystem","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/scheduledsystem","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScheduledSystem"}],"title":"ScheduledSystem","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ScheduledSystem"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/Schedule":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/Schedule","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/schedule","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A list of systems that run on a world, in order, and at the same time where they can."}],"title":"Schedule","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Schedule","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://Systems/documentation/Systems/ForwardChanges":{"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Systems\/documentation\/Systems\/ForwardChanges","url":"\/documentation\/systems\/forwardchanges","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ForwardChanges"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A system that yields each component of one type added or changed since it last ran to an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"asynchronous stream, with its entity."}],"title":"ForwardChanges","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ForwardChanges"}]},"doc://WorldModule/documentation/WorldModule/Query":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Query"}],"title":"Query","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Query"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/WorldModule\/documentation\/WorldModule\/Query","abstract":[{"text":"A description of the entities to visit and the components to read from each.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/worldmodule\/query","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"doc